Z||000011||ThatRickGuy||08-24-2000||11:20 AM||||well, start from the bigining.<BR>Does the batter have juice?<BR>Do you hear any noise at all when you turn the key (the fuel pump humm, the solinoid click, starter clatter)?<BR>Are there blown fuses?<BR>are there scorch marks on the out side of the computer case? (usually a bad sign)<BR>I'm still adjusting to the computerized car world, so I'm not sure from there. I'd say check the error codes, but if the battery is good and you're not getting any juice to the computer, well, it can't be good.||||reg||1
Z||000012||theogre||08-24-2000||11:25 AM||||That kind of dead usually ain't the ECM. Usually a fuse link or cable fried.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Alex4mula||08-24-2000||11:37 AM||||I would check your battery before spending in a computer. Specially if nothing electrical works... ||||reg||1
Z||000014||whamel||08-24-2000||11:39 AM||||    Where in MI are you?  (e-mail me if you like.)  Maybe we can take a look at it together or something.<BR>     By the way, my Buick did a similar thing (floor it -&gt; cough, cough) and had a maladjusted TV cable.  It took it about 3 months to completely eat the transmission again.  I guess I know what caused it to kill the last one too now.||||reg||1
